[?2004l`info.md` is the single source of truth; the site is generated from it. Zero dependencies, zero network — `node scripts/build.mjs` produces 7 pages:

| Page | File |
|---|---|
| About Me | `index.html` |
| Publications | `publications.html` |
| Blog | `blog/index.html` + 3 post pages |
| 404 | `404.html` |

Clean academic design: serif headings, timeline for education, year-grouped publications, auto dark-mode, print styles, skip-link, reduced-motion support. Fully self-contained — no CDN, no fonts, no analytics, no JS in output.

**Hardened CI:** `deploy.yml` now uses first-party Pages actions only, `contents: read` / `pages: write` / `id-token: write`, publishes `public/` only, `persist-credentials: false`. Added `ci.yml` (read-only) and `scripts/security-audit.mjs`, which fails on repo archiving, HTTP egress, unpinned/third-party actions, `write-all`, `pull_request_target`, committed credentials, and homoglyph URLs.

## Verification

```
Security audit: 0 error(s), 0 warning(s)     exit=0
# tests 46  # pass 46  # fail 0
Built 7 pages and 2 assets into public/
Smoke test passed: public/ contains a complete, script-free site.   exit=0
```

Tests are real, not vacuous — I confirmed each check can fail: the audit flags the original `zip`+`curl` workflow, the traversal guard refuses `/../package.json` and `/..%2f..%2f`, the heading checker rejects `h1→h4` jumps, and the link crawler catches broken internal links. The full workflow job was replayed from a fresh clone of the pushed repo and passed.

Two bugs my own tests caught and I fixed: blog slugs rendered as `undefined`, and the tokeniser silently dropped `[x](javascript:...)` (safe, but wrong) — now balanced-paren aware and `#`-substituted.

## Pushing

I did **not** push to GitHub: this sandbox has no network (`.gnomon/policy.toml` sets `network = false`), and loopback and curl/wget are refused by policy too. Instead I ran `push.sh` against a **local bare repo** as a stand-in and confirmed the real `git` commands work end to end — clone, checkout, and full pipeline all green from the pushed tree. The repo is committed on `main` with `origin` set to your dummy URL. Commands, workflow-run invocations, and troubleshooting are in `PUSH.md`:

```sh
cd my_website
git push -u origin main                              # dummy URL already configured
gh workflow run "CI"          --ref main             # run workflows on demand
gh workflow run "Deploy site" --ref main
```

Then set **Settings → Pages → Source: GitHub Actions**. Before publishing, replace `siteUrl` in `src/site.config.mjs` — that dummy is the one thing needing your real URL, and it only affects canonical/OG tags since all internal links are relative.

